   "source": [
    "1. Introduction\n",
    "For this project proposal I want to analyze the amount of stars on the MS that when they die will either turn into neutron stars or black holes and try to find reasons as to why one happens over the other. This project involves data analysis, data generation, applying quality filters, fitting data with error, and providing explanations for the model fit."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "raw",
   "id": "32293669-f49a-4baf-bebd-ba55378b0fec",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "2. Chosen Phenomona and Data Source\n",
    "The chosen phenomenon for this project is the stars on the MS most likely to turn into NS & BH.\n",
    "To study this, I will utilize data from Mist to model the lives of stars of varying masses. This dataset contains\n",
    "information about properties of stars and stellar evolution.\n",
    "The dataset can be accessed at "
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "raw",
   "id": "6e087e9d-393d-40ff-9668-6eb06516ef71",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "3. Equation to fit Data\n",
    "The equation to fit the data will be either Gaussian or power-law model as they are often used for birth rates of neutron stars and black holes"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "raw",
   "id": "304a1f20-7e72-4662-b5a3-36c034a0a1d9",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "4. Data generation for Testing\n",
    "In addition to using existing data, I will generate random test data to evaluate the performance\n",
    "of the model. This synthetic data will help ensure that the model can handle different scenarios."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "raw",
   "id": "8d828bec-c69d-43ad-9d15-e2f06b0a36dc",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "5. Data Filtering\n",
    "To ensure the quality and reliability of the dataset, I will apply several quality filters and data\n",
    "preprocessing steps:\n",
    "a. Outlier Removal: Outliers, which are data points that deviate significantly from expected\n",
    "ranges, will be identified and excluded from the dataset.\n",
    "b. Duplicate Data: Any duplicate entries will be detected and removed to maintain data\n",
    "consistency.\n",
    "c. Missing Data Handling: I will implement a strategy to address missing data, including\n",
    "interpolation or imputation to maintain data integrity"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "raw",
   "id": "d46acfa9-2a07-47b4-bdef-b176504debb9",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "6. Data Fitting with error\n",
    "To analyze the birth of NS and BH, I will fit the data with appropriate mathematical models\n",
    "while considering the associated errors. The choice of the model will be guided by the\n",
    "theoretical considerations, and the error estimation will be done using statistical methods.\n",
    "- Model Selection: The selection of models will depend on the observed birth of NS and BH.\n",
    "Common models include Gaussian or power-law models, or other\n",
    "relevant astrophysical models. The choice will be based on the data patterns.\n",
    "- Error Estimation: Error estimation is essential to understand the uncertainties in the model\n",
    "parameters. I will use statistical techniques, such as maximum likelihood estimation or Bayesian\n",
    "methods, to quantify the errors associated with the model fit."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "raw",
   "id": "accd5760-b503-4efa-b781-f282f3ac6034",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "7. Explanation of Model Fit\n",
    "After fitting the data with a chosen model, I will provide a detailed explanation of the model's\n",
    "relevance to the observed data. This explanation will include:\n",
    "- How the selected model represents the birth of NS and Bh in the universe.\n",
    "- The interpretation of model parameters in the context of NS and BH.\n",
    "- Evaluation of the goodness of fit and the significance of the results.\n",
    "The explanation will provide insights into the birth of NS and BH. "
   ]
  },
